---
// "Beware of impersonators" block, shown above the footer on every page.
---
<section class="relative bg-[#0a0a0f] px-6 lg:px-8 pt-10" aria-labelledby="impersonation-title">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <div class="flex items-start gap-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-300/20 bg-amber-300/[0.04] px-5 py-4">
      <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-300/80 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z" />
      </svg>
      <div>
        <h2 id="impersonation-title" class="text-white mb-1" style="font-family:'Montserrat',sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:700">Beware of impersonators</h2>
        <p class="text-white/55" style="font-size:13px;line-height:1.7">
          Scammers sometimes pretend to be recovery companies, including ScamHelp. All emails, contracts and payment requests from us come only from @scamhelp.net addresses, and payments are made only to Transparent Business Solutions B.V. We will never claim to have already recovered your funds or ask you to pay to release them. If you are unsure, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@scamhelp.net" class="text-[#9ACF84] hover:underline">support@scamhelp.net</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
